<https://github.com/PodComet/ICoN-PCL-Equipment-Metadata/id/reference-link/LINK-SW17-345FAF5977C4> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Source reports this apparatus type in its manufacturing or characterization workflow. A segmented-flow platform produces cesium lead halide nanocrystals while recording fluorescence. CETONI neMESYS syringe pumps feed precursor and carrier streams to a PEEK cross. Droplets travel through heated coiled tubing, then an optical flow cell. Custom LabVIEW software sequences conditions and acquires data." .
<https://github.com/PodComet/ICoN-PCL-Equipment-Metadata/id/reference-link/LINK-SW17-345FAF5977C4> <https://github.com/PodComet/ICoN-PCL-Equipment-Metadata/ontology#relation> "supports_claim" .
<https://github.com/PodComet/ICoN-PCL-Equipment-Metadata/id/reference-link/LINK-SW17-345FAF5977C4> <https://github.com/PodComet/ICoN-PCL-Equipment-Metadata/ontology#reviewStatus> "claim_checked" .
<https://github.com/PodComet/ICoN-PCL-Equipment-Metadata/id/reference-link/LINK-SW17-345FAF5977C4> <https://github.com/PodComet/ICoN-PCL-Equipment-Metadata/ontology#scope> "Precursor preparation and material handling are source-specific research descriptions, not a general SOP. Carrier phase and precursor solvents are distinct roles; no implicit recipe transfer to other P classes. Photon counters and spectrometers are inline characterization; do not present them as synthesis hardware. No maker star, photo, price or exact neMESYS subtype verified in this research task. M-class placement is curator interpretation; no unnamed commercial model is validated." .
