<https://github.com/PodComet/ICoN-PCL-Equipment-Metadata/id/reference-link/LINK-SW17-8A531F606633> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Source reports this apparatus type in its manufacturing or characterization workflow. Electrospinning a hydroxyapatite/PAN precursor followed by nitrogen-atmosphere carbonization produces hydroxyapatite-containing carbon nanofibers. The BTF-1200C vacuum tube furnace is expressly named. Further preparation incorporates myoglobin and Nafion into an electrode coating. The electrospinner is not identified by make/model." .
<https://github.com/PodComet/ICoN-PCL-Equipment-Metadata/id/reference-link/LINK-SW17-8A531F606633> <https://github.com/PodComet/ICoN-PCL-Equipment-Metadata/ontology#relation> "supports_claim" .
<https://github.com/PodComet/ICoN-PCL-Equipment-Metadata/id/reference-link/LINK-SW17-8A531F606633> <https://github.com/PodComet/ICoN-PCL-Equipment-Metadata/ontology#reviewStatus> "claim_checked" .
<https://github.com/PodComet/ICoN-PCL-Equipment-Metadata/id/reference-link/LINK-SW17-8A531F606633> <https://github.com/PodComet/ICoN-PCL-Equipment-Metadata/ontology#scope> "P11 is the broad thermal-conversion route. Do not label this as the same protocol as P20: HAp-loaded PAN carbonization differs from nanocarbon-loaded polymer-mat electrospinning. Hydroxyapatite is a phosphate; do not mislabel it as a metal oxide. M-class placement is curator interpretation; no unnamed commercial model is validated." .
