<https://github.com/PodComet/ICoN-PCL-Equipment-Metadata/id/reference-link/LINK-SW17-BD3CA629F75D> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Repeated phosphorus insertion and oxidative extraction converts Pd seed nanocrystals to hollow Pd nanoshells. The authors describe heated magnetic stirring, centrifugation/washing and unspecified sonication. Repeating the conversion enlarges voids and thins shells. Atmosphere and temperature alter the observed morphology; this is a reported study result, not an app prediction." .
<https://github.com/PodComet/ICoN-PCL-Equipment-Metadata/id/reference-link/LINK-SW17-BD3CA629F75D> <https://github.com/PodComet/ICoN-PCL-Equipment-Metadata/ontology#relation> "supports_claim" .
<https://github.com/PodComet/ICoN-PCL-Equipment-Metadata/id/reference-link/LINK-SW17-BD3CA629F75D> <https://github.com/PodComet/ICoN-PCL-Equipment-Metadata/ontology#reviewStatus> "claim_checked" .
<https://github.com/PodComet/ICoN-PCL-Equipment-Metadata/id/reference-link/LINK-SW17-BD3CA629F75D> <https://github.com/PodComet/ICoN-PCL-Equipment-Metadata/ontology#scope> "No named manufacturing maker/model; do not create a commercial instrument identity. Sonication does not resolve probe versus bath; do not claim either exact model. Three-neck flask and nitrogen flow do not independently establish a Schlenk manifold. Named TEM, XRD, ICP-MS and electrochemical apparatus are characterization/catalytic testing, separate from manufacture. One published source used two atomistic and experimental analyses; not independent validation of app predictions. P-class maps the stated source stage, not all alternative ontology steps." .
<https://github.com/PodComet/ICoN-PCL-Equipment-Metadata/id/reference-link/LINK-SW17-BD3CA629F75D> <https://github.com/PodComet/ICoN-PCL-Equipment-Metadata/ontology#sourceLocator> "Methods / Synthesis of Pd nanocubes; Methods / Synthesis of hollow Pd nanocrystals" .
